## 2. What this rules out / what is left

# Ruled out: temporal accumulation in the menu (history is discarded every frame).
# Still open: (a) the jitter offset fed to DLSS vs the panorama's actual sub-pixel
# offset (a sign/scale mismatch would shift the image by 2*jitter every frame, i.e.
# vertical judder); (b) DLSS spatial upscaling itself on a low-res rotating panorama;
# (c) the menu's own presentation cadence, independent of which upscaler runs.
# Next: A/B in the menu - same background with TAAU restored vs DLSS suppressed -
# to separate (a/b) from (c). No new build needed.
